  "notes": "Amazon listing B08M5WJXQ8 re-read 2026-08-26: 'ZKYMZL 30W LED Moving Head DJ Lights DMX512 GOBO Spotlight with 8 Colors + Color-Split Effect 8 Rotating Patterns'. Description spec block: AC100-240V, 30W, beam angle 15 deg, 9/11CH, 0-100% electronic dimming, manual focus, item size 159 x 146 x 247 mm (6.3 x 5.71 x 9.75 in; the dimension image agrees: 6.3 in wide, 9.75 in tall), 5.6 lb (2.54 kg); 3-pin DMX in/out, 4-digit display. Physical now uses the listing's bare-fixture figures (was 210 x 260 x 280 mm / 3.2 kg, which the shipped manual gives as 280 x 210 x 260 mm / 3.4 kg -- probably boxed). The listing's 'Product guides and documents' User Manual (PDF) is the same Amazon-hosted manual already cited (81ej8MIZpBL.pdf); it says beam angle 11 deg and 540/180 deg pan/tilt, so 11 deg is kept (listing text says 15 deg; one bullet claims 270 deg tilt but the description, image and manual all say 180). 9/11ch chart from that manual: 11ch = Pan, Pan fine, Tilt, Tilt fine, Colour (0-127 select, 128-189 rotate fast>slow, 190-193 stop, 194-255 rotate slow>fast), Gobo (0-63 select, 64-127 shake, 128-189 rotate, 190-193 stop, 194-255 rotate), Shutter/strobe (0-7 off, 8-15 open, 16-131 strobe slow>fast, 132-139 open, 140-181 fast-close/slow-open, 182-189 open, 190-231 fast-open/slow-close, 232-239 open, 240-247 random, 248-255 open), Dimmer 0-100%, P/T speed fast>slow, Function (70-79 blackout on P/T move, 90-99 blackout on colour, 110-119 blackout on gobo, 200-209 reset), Dimmer modes (0-20 standard, 21-40 stage, 61-80 architectural, 81-100 theatre, 101-255 default). The repo channel map (Pan, Tilt, Colour wheel, Gobo, Shutter, Dimmer at offsets 0/2/4/5/6/7) matches; the manual gives no per-colour slot values inside 0-127 so the repo's 8-step slot centres remain an inference. Colour names from the OFL Lixada profile."
